A||N||4||FieroSTETZ||help! oil all over the passenger side floor!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-06-2001||11:47 AM||||i think it might be the heater core, laid out a piece of paper and its getting oily dripping on it, in about 5 minutes the whole paper was saturated. sounds like the heater core? is there any way i can disconnect it? I have a 9 hour drive after work tonight and no time to make a repair. havent needed the heater in 2 years, so shouldnt need it for the next few days. any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-06-2001||11:51 AM||||Sure sounds like the heater core!  Thats what usually leaks into the passenger foot well.  I think you can access the two tubes that go to it from inside the hood.  You'd have to have a short peice of pipe to clamp them together to bypass the heater core.  If you leave it connected on a 9 hour drive, you'd better bring a lot of paper towels and a few extra bottles of coolant... good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||10-06-2001||12:41 PM||||That stinks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Like Fformula88 said just splice the 2 lines together in the front compartment, bypassing the heater core.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||10-06-2001||01:57 PM||||I just took the hoses off the heater core in the front compartment.  They are right behind the windshield washer reservoir.  Since they're two different size hoses, splicing them is a bit difficult.  I got a heater hose splicing kit from Pep Boys and then wrapped electrical tape around the end for the bigger hose to build it up some.  I've been driving it like that for about a month with no problems.  Just got my new heater core this week, so if the rain will let up, that's my project for this weekend!||||reg||14
Z||000004||ka4nkf||10-06-2001||08:55 PM||||Go to Auto Zone and look where they have the thermostats and you will find heater block off caps. you need a 5/8 and a 3/4 I blocked mine off under the car but you can do it under the hood. also I think I saw them At Advance auto also. It sure makes it easy. also you will need two clamps.||||reg||1
